   "daf": "116a",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "תַּנְיָא כְּווֹתֵיהּ דְּרַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: תַּבְלִין זֵכֶר לַתֶּבֶן, חֲרוֹסֶת זֵכֶר לַטִּיט. אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בְּרַבִּי צָדוֹק, כָּךְ הָיוּ אוֹמְרִים תַּגָּרֵי חָרָךְ שֶׁבִּירוּשָׁלַיִם: בּוֹאוּ וּטְלוּ לָכֶם תַּבְלִין לְמִצְוָה.",
   "en": "It «was taught» in a baraita «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yoḥanan:» The «spices» used in the ḥaroset are «in remembrance of the hay» that our forefathers used for building in Egypt, and the «ḥaroset» itself «is in remembrance of the mortar. Rabbi Elazar, son of Rabbi Tzadok, said:» When selling ḥaroset, «the small shopkeepers in Jerusalem would say as follows: Come and take spices for yourselves for» the «mitzva.»"
  }
 ],
